                            <comment id="16055426" author="ezhuravl" created="Tue, 20 Jun 2017 09:18:56 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Tc: &lt;a href=&quot;http://ci.ignite.apache.org/project.html?projectId=Ignite20Tests&amp;amp;branch_Ignite20Tests=pull%2F2158%2Fhead&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;http://ci.ignite.apache.org/project.html?projectId=Ignite20Tests&amp;amp;branch_Ignite20Tests=pull%2F2158%2Fhead&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;PR: &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/2158&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/2158&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16055481" author="sboikov" created="Tue, 20 Jun 2017 09:51:41 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hi,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;First, you did not add test in suite, this means it is not run on TC.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In description I see &quot;can return false and reschedule rebalancing&quot;, I do not understand how your patch fix this, please explain what was wrong and how it was fixed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Also I tried to run test from your patch without fix, and it still pass, I think more reliable test is needed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Thanks&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16057533" author="ezhuravl" created="Wed, 21 Jun 2017 13:40:14 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hi Semen,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Thanks for your comments, &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I added test to the test suite.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Actually, it was a misunderstanding of root of a problem. False returns when new rebalance for this cache already in queue. So, in this case it was not a rescheduled rebalancing, it was another rebalance that was invoked manually.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I rewrited test, now it&apos;s failing without patch.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16058867" author="sboikov" created="Thu, 22 Jun 2017 06:56:24 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Merged into master.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
